# The package signing trust root of ArchPOWER, for its three ports.
#
# ArchPOWER signs with keys that archlinux-keyring does not have. This pin
# gives the keyring package, its sha256 and its trusted keys, so SigLevel =
# Required stays on. The fields are in archlinuxarm.pin.
#
# ⭐ One pin for the three ports. The keyring package has the architecture
# `any`, and the trust root is the same for the three.
#
# The package is in [base-any] (path base/any on the origin), not in the
# database of an architecture.
#
# ⚠ The origin and its read-through proxy answer HTTP 403 to GitHub runner
# addresses. The package is in this directory, so the build does not need them.
#
# ⚠ 5E8F266C9F31E41DEBFBDC7C80701B1A8BC1A35B is in the keyring and not in the
# pin. It is the master key of the keyring, not in archpower-trusted, and it
# signs no package.
#
# ⚠ 3B40CFA2B2FC99268DE7B31BF95FE1C7E212CF15 is in archpower-revoked and not in
# the keyring. install-port-keyring installs the revoked list too, so pacman
# refuses a package that this key signed.
#
# To read the values again, on a host with bsdtar and gpg:
#   curl -sSfL --connect-timeout 15 --max-time 120 -o k.pkg.tar.zst <mirror>/<package>
#   sha256sum k.pkg.tar.zst
#   bsdtar -xOf k.pkg.tar.zst usr/share/pacman/keyrings/archpower-trusted
#   bsdtar -xOf k.pkg.tar.zst usr/share/pacman/keyrings/archpower.gpg | \
#     gpg --with-colons --show-keys
#
# Adopted 2026-08-28. Verified on that date against a mirror line below.

keyring = archpower
arch    = powerpc powerpc64 powerpc64le
mirror  = https://ghcr.mirror.archlinux.pkgforge.dev/powerpc64le/base-any
mirror  = https://repo.archlinuxpower.org/base/any
mirror  = https://api.rv.pkgforge.dev/https://repo.archlinuxpower.org/base/any
package = archpower-keyring-20260408-1-any.pkg.tar.zst
sha256  = 2f3ebb1a9234775e9244bf45ae1121a20bdbe7d27efbd440a3da172a2baf6241
trusted = 8D3D6CE8D4F0625F4D7109022205B7A06C2656A3 2032-01-03
trusted = D201F92AE42528456537C3F9B96775F34689694C 2031-02-22
trusted = DE9D1B4851C66CCD9994459CFBB374D5D026D9DA 2031-04-06
